 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Lots of people do, and there's no law against it. Just make sure to stand up every hour or so, and move around more than you might have. Then it's probably doing more good than harm. Just be aware that sitting is the enemy, and get up every hour or so. Then try a standing desk, or set your seat so you' leaning slightly forward and your feet can touch the floor. A good mattress helps, and a pillow under your lower back can be useful. A gentle bend in your knees is also good for your spine.",
